<newsitem itemid="89512" id="root" date="1996-10-01" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Lloyd Thompson year pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Lloyd Thompson year pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr  (pence)		16.8		   vs 16.3</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  10.0		   vs 9.0</p>
<p> Pretax profit	     21.6		   vs 20.4</p>
<p> Investment income	 7.4		    vs 6.2</p>
<p> Brokerage income	  48.4		   vs 45.0</p>
<p> Expenses		    34.2		   vs 30.8</p>
<p> Exceptional		 16.2		   vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Lloyd Thompson Group, the international insurance and reinsurance broker said exceptional items were a provision for the anticipated contribution to Lloyd's reconstruction and renewal plan, a charge for settling litigation and a provision for continuing costs of surplus property.</p>
<p>&quot;We are pleased with progress in the first three months of the current year in the face of very difficult market conditions. Our strategy of developing geographically, expanding our direct business and entering new areas by recruiting individuals and acquiring smaller companies continues to yield financial benefits,&quot; the group said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
